          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.735,
            0.882,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Which of the following lengths can be the sidelengths of a triangle? Explain your answers. Note that for each set, the three lengths have the same unit of measure.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.129,
            0.8,
            0.181,
            0.817
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.828,
            0.266,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) 2, 2, 5",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.857,
            0.363,
            0.873
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Since 2 + 2 < 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.21,
            0.879,
            0.666,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, these are not the side lengths of a triangle."
            }
          ]
